{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אלה מסעי", :translit "eleh mas'ei", :gloss "These are the journeys"} {:he "מוצאיהם למסעיהם", :translit "motza'eihem lemas'eihem", :gloss "their departures according to their journeys"} {:he "ואלה מסעיהם למוצאיהם", :translit "ve'eleh mas'eihem lemotsa'eihem", :gloss "and these are their journeys according to their departures"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Literary observation: the verse reverses the order of 'departures' and 'journeys' to signal symmetry."}], :frame {:text "Numbers 33:1–2 records: 'These are the journeys (מסעי) of the children of Israel… And Moses wrote their departures (מוצאיהם) according to their journeys (למסעיהם).' The phrase 'by the mouth of HaShem' (על פי ה') appears repeatedly in Numbers 33:2 to describe the Israelites' travels. Ba'al HaTurim notes the reversed word order between the two verses and connects it to this refrain, indicating divine direction of every movement.", :sources ["Numbers 33:1" "Numbers 33:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Literary observation: the verse reverses the order of 'departures' and 'journeys' to signal symmetry.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:31.750192165Z", :model "glm-5.2"}